{
 "scene_id": "04.2",
 "poem": "04",
 "title": "Nevermore",
 "movement": "FOLDED WHISPERS",
 "seconds": 14,
 "lines": "the waves will / calm to folded whispers / & the winds / will mute the trees / for the right / level of silence / to find a throbbing heart / left at the midlife / corner we turn toward / the incline\u2014 / a familiar heart / which has shaken / off every / sad blue note / life can perform / to overcome / & spread inspiration / & it used to be mine. / I'll lift it with care, / putting it back in place. / & tell myself / nevermore\u2014",
